  "hevc_recorder_fix": {
    "headline": "8K, 4K120 and long/sustained 4K60 now record a decodable HEVC track; previously they crashed the writer or wrote a non-decodable track.",
    "patches": [
      "patches/evolution/nezha-hevc-length-prefixed-nal.patch",
      "patches/evolution/nezha-hevc-recorder-csd-duplicate.patch",
      "patches/evolution/nezha-hevc-recorder-csd-annexb.patch"
    ],
    "cause": "The Xiaomi recorder enables vendor.qti-ext-enc-nal-length-bs, so the vendor encoder emits length-prefixed NAL units and length-prefixed codec-specific data. The AOSP MPEG4Writer parsed those as Annex-B, which underflowed a NAL size (FORTIFY crash) or built a malformed hvcC.",
